  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: PatApp_5
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "The research team contacts you to complete a survey about your day-to-day
    life after receiving the trial treatment. They ask about things like fatigue,
    pain, or how easy it is to do your normal activities. These patient-reported
    outcomes (PROs) give researchers information that trial data and lab tests alone
    can\u2019t provide.\r\n\r\nWhat is the main purpose of patient-reported outcomes
    (PROs)?\r"
  explanation: Patient-reported outcomes (PROs) highlight the human side of treatment
    by capturing how patients actually feel and function during and after care. These
    insights go beyond lab results and clinical measures, showing how a treatment
    impacts daily life, well-being, and quality of life. By including PROs, research
    becomes more patient-centered and better reflects the real-life impact of new
    treatments.
  correctAnswer: "To understand the patient\u2019s personal experience with treatment
    and quality of life"
  incorrectAnswer1: To record how many patients participated in each phase of the
    trial
  incorrectAnswer2: To ensure that patients are continuing to take the new medicine
    correctly
  incorrectAnswer3: To help researchers predict how safe and effective this new treatment
    will be
  questionRole: Patient
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: Approval
